From: Proton GE Team <proton-ge@example.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 21:05:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Clear pending pause when playing after scrub.

When Play is requested while both a scrub and a pause are pending, the
non-zero rate transition starts the media session but leaves the Media Engine
pause-pending flag set.  Frames advance, but MESessionStarted therefore does
not emit MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_EVENT_PLAYING.  AVPro waits for that event and
reports an unknown playback error after its startup timeout.

The pending play is the latest requested state.  Clear the superseded pause
state when completing the scrub and starting playback.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1154,1 +1154,2 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_session_events_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *ifac
-                        media_engine_set_flag(engine, FLAGS_ENGINE_PLAY_PENDING, FALSE);
+                        media_engine_set_flag(engine, FLAGS_ENGINE_PLAY_PENDING | FLAGS_ENGINE_PAUSE_PENDING
+                                | FLAGS_ENGINE_PAUSED, FALSE);
